<title>USA: U.S. Feb industrial output rose 0.5 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Feb industrial output rose 0.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Board report of U.S. industrial production and capacity utilization, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p> Total Industrial:	  Feb    Jan    Dec    Nov   Feb97/96</p>
<p> Production, Pct Change   0.5   -0.1    0.4    0.8    3.8</p>
<p> Previous Estimates		 UNCH    0.5    0.8</p>
<p> Production Index-X     118.1  117.6  117.7  117.2</p>
<p> -				Feb    Jan    Dec    Nov   Feb96</p>
<p> Pct of Capacity Use     83.3   83.2    83.5  83.4   83.2</p>
<p> Previous Estimates		 83.3    83.5  83.4</p>
<p>X--1987 equals 100.</p>
<p>Industrial Production,Seasonally adjusted percent changes:</p>
<p> -				Feb    Jan    Dec    Nov  Feb97/96</p>
<p> Major Market Products    0.5    UNCH   0.2    1.1    3.6</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods	    UNCH  -0.6    0.4    1.3    2.1</p>
<p> -Business Equipment	1.1    1.0    0.5    0.8    7.0</p>
<p> -Construc.Supplies	 1.4    UNCH  -2.2    2.6    5.7</p>
<p> Major Materials	    0.5   -0.3    0.8    0.4    4.1</p>
<p> Manufacturing Industry   0.8   -0.2    0.6    0.8    4.4</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	     1.2    0.1    0.4    1.0    5.6</p>
<p> --Primary Metals	   2.3   -1.2    0.6   -2.9    5.2</p>
<p> --Autos/Light Trucks     0.7    2.5    0.1    7.1    4.1</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods	 0.3   -0.6    0.8    0.5    3.0</p>
<p> --Petroleum Products     0.7   -0.6   -0.1   -0.9    1.3</p>
<p> Mining Industry	    1.3   -0.6    1.4    0.1    4.8</p>
<p> Utilities Industry	-3.5    1.3   -1.6    2.4   -2.8</p>
<p>Percent of Capacity: Manufacturing, Mining, Utilities:</p>
<p>    (Seasonally Adj.)     Feb    Jan    Dec    Nov   Feb'96</p>
<p> Manufacturing	     82.5   82.1   82.5   82.4   82.2</p>
<p>Percent of Capacity: Manufacturing, Mining, Utilities:</p>
<p>    (Seasonally Adj.)     Feb    Jan    Dec    Nov   Feb'96</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	    82.0   81.4   81.7   81.9   82.4</p>
<p> --Primary Metals	  91.2   89.4   90.7   90.5   89.8</p>
<p> --Autos/Light Trucks    80.1   79.6   77.8   77.8   78.0</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods	83.1   82.9   83.5   82.9   82.0</p>
<p> --Petroleum Products    94.3   93.7   94.3   94.4   93.5</p>
<p> Mining			92.9   91.7   92.4   91.1   88.5</p>
<p> Utilities		   87.1   90.4   89.3   91.0   91.5</p>
<p>Motor vehicle assemblies rose slightly in February to a rate of 6.1 million a year for cars from 6.0 million in January. For light trucks the assembly rate was down to 6.0 million from 6.1 million.</p>
<p>The Fed said the increase in overall February industrial output resulted from more production of durable consumer goods, business equipment, construction supplies and durable materials.</p>
<p>It said production of energy products and materials dipped sharply because of unseasonably warm weather during February that reduced utility demand.</p>
